From: EL10 Compatibility Patch
Subject: [PATCH] el10: Force sd_varlink_server_listen_address mode to 0666

EL10's libsystemd 257 implements sd_varlink_server_listen_address() with
a mode_t parameter and validates that (mode & ~0777) == 0. Newer systemd
headers define SD_VARLINK_SERVER_MODE_MKDIR_0755 with a high bit set
(0x40000000), which fails this validation with EINVAL.

Force the mode to 0666 directly to ensure compatibility with EL10's
runtime libsystemd regardless of the systemd-devel version used to compile.

diff --git a/daemon/gdm-dynamic-user-store.c b/daemon/gdm-dynamic-user-store.c
--- a/daemon/gdm-dynamic-user-store.c
+++ b/daemon/gdm-dynamic-user-store.c
@@ -39,10 +39,9 @@

-#ifndef SD_VARLINK_SERVER_MODE_MKDIR_0755
-#define SD_VARLINK_SERVER_MODE_MKDIR_0755 0
-#endif
+/* Force 0666: EL10 libsystemd 257 rejects any mode bits outside 0777 */
+#undef SD_VARLINK_SERVER_MODE_MKDIR_0755
+#define SD_VARLINK_SERVER_MODE_MKDIR_0755 0
